From: pokeplatinum-3ds <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 23:35:40 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] The buildings' sun shadows in parts, merged, and on higher
 ground (SDK_PORT_3DS)

A building's sun shadow is now a hull for each group of its model's
polygons that touch (NitroPort_Gx3dShadowHullParts, up to 8): one hull
of the whole model laid the Day Care's house, sheds and yard under one
shadow. A group that is mostly open (a fence round a yard) casts none.

Each is one even shade, a tree's (26 of 31): where a tree's shadow lies
in a building's, the two are one shadow, not a darker tree cut out of it.

And where the ground under its corners is higher than the building
stands (a tower in a dip, the Galactic building's dishes in their pits:
the shadow was under it), a second copy is laid at that height. The
field gives the ground (TerrainCollisionManager) while it draws its maps:
MapProp_PortGround, around LandDataManager_RenderLoadedMaps.
---
